# Frontend formatting scope.
#
# HTML is excluded on evidence rather than taste.  Running Prettier over the frontend
# documents is not content-neutral:
#   - the format-equivalence check reported 4 of them as content-changed and
#     8 as having inter-tag whitespace changes, because Prettier inserts newlines
#     inside <button>/<p> text nodes (this changes `textContent`);
#   - even with `htmlWhitespaceSensitivity: strict` the two large documents still
#     get long Chinese text runs wrapped, and a wrap between CJK characters
#     renders as a space that the original markup never had.
# SPA 迁移后页面文档只剩两处，同样按「原样保留」处理：
#   - index.html          —— SPA 唯一入口（外壳）；
#   - src/views/*.vue     —— 由原 8 个 pages/*.html 的 <body> 抽取而来，
#                            模板与旧标记逐字节等价，是上面结论的直接继承者。
frontend/index.html
frontend/src/views/*.vue

# Third-party bundles stay byte-identical to upstream, exactly as the
# de-obfuscation tooling already treats them (report/imports walkers skip
# `vendor`).  Reformatting minified vendor code would be pure noise.
frontend/public/static/vendor/
